     "explanation": "Horowitz's point is not that education is useless but that it is necessarily general, while the CEO's actual problems are always specific to one company's people, market, and moment. He argues the gap can only be closed through active, ongoing self-education combining targeted reading, peer networks, honest retrospection, and direct immersion in the business.",
